TrialSieve redistributes derived data. This file names what, from where, and
under which terms.

## Synthea sample data

`panel.jsonl.gz` is derived from the Synthea sample FHIR R4 archive published by
MITRE. The source URL, the archive sha256, the byte count and the selection rule
are recorded in `panel_provenance.json` beside this file, so the derivation is
checkable rather than described.

    Synthea (TM) synthetic patient generator and sample data
    Copyright 2017-2021 The MITRE Corporation
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The data are synthetic. No real patient, and no real identifier, appears in
them. The derivative in this repository is redistributed under the same Apache
License, Version 2.0, and this notice is carried with it as that licence asks.
The selection applied was: alive at the index date and aged 18 or over. Nothing
else was filtered, and the counts of what that removed are in
`panel_provenance.json`.

## ClinicalTrials.gov

`trials/` and `trials_index.json` are responses from ClinicalTrials.gov API v2,
a United States Government work in the public domain. `trials_index.json`
records the API version and the retrieval date. The three protocols are public
registrations and are reproduced as returned.

## Terminology catalogue

`terminology_catalog.json` was derived from the same pinned Synthea archive
before the panel was cut, and carries the same Apache-2.0 terms. `REPRODUCE.md`
states plainly that nothing in this repository regenerates it, because the
source bundles are not vendored.
